Z||000011||dave||05-19-99||12:49 AM||||I feel I know a lot about various audio formats, as i have done exstensive research and own many different formats, (cd, mp3, dat and mini-disc)and I almost consider myself an Audiophile.   I also think MP3's are great, they're easy to find, they sound decent and they don't skip.  But after reading the raves about their sound quality on this board (especially being better than the original, cd!), i thought i should inform you that there is no possibile way that a MP3 could sound BETTER than a Cd, in fact Mp3s have the WORST sound quality amongs cd, mp3, dat, but they are a LOT better than tapes!.  Mp3's use a 'lossy' compression (they block out frequencies which are masked by loud frequencies and decrease the range of frequencies; if a bass note over powered a guitar string, then it will delete the guitar string from the note, only leaving the bass) <br>Mp3s compress the music 1:12, this can only be achieved by deleting and altering the music.  With this in mind, there is no conceiveable way that a copy 1/12th the size of the original, could sound better than the original.  I've read numerous sound comparasons about Mp3s and the bulk of them absolutely trash them for their sound-quality .  I own 2 mini- disc players/recorders, a mp3-player, a dat recorder and a very high quality cd-player, when i play back all the formats i can instantly spot the mp3, the sound is much flatter, boomier and it looses some of it's fidelity, the other formats are only distinguisable from cd at when doing side-side listening to certail notes through high quality headphones/speakers.  I think mp3's will remain the #1 computer format and they are an excellent contender for portable audio, but they should be ignored if your concerned about the quality of your music.  If your looking for an alternative for a CD-deck, Consider mini-disc, they offer re-recordabilty, 10 or 40 sec shock, 74 mins, and they are durable, they have a compression of 1/5, but the chip used to compress (called ATRAC) has been constantly upgraded over the last 7 years, the latest version of ATRAC is indistinguishable from CD.<p>
Z||000012||yellowFormula||05-19-99||07:34 PM||||Talking about Mp3's and sound quality etc., I did some reasearch on the topic and I put my money into Mini-Discs. They sound exactly like CD's, and if you have a home Cd player wiht a digital optical output it will be EXACTLY like a CD if analyzed by a computer.  I considered the CD recorder but I will wait a year or two to let them get the bugs out.  Oh and by the way , go with Infinity Kappa speakers! They are in a league of their own when it comes to car audio!  
