Z||000014||lowCG||06-01-99||02:06 PM||||Way cool page here.One thing that made a big difference after installing the upper end of an MBQuart system(4"+tweeters+crossovers) under the grills on my dash was to aim the tweeters(mounted on metal straps) such that the right hand side could be best heard by the left ear,and visaversa.the speaker location was intended to allow the windshield to reflect the sound.By doing this, you get the effect of a theater.Probably need to use a crossover to "pad" down the tweeters so you don't ruin your ears too! Made a (8")bass cabinet that fits snug under the passengers dash,speaker facing downward;not using an aftermarket glove box.I can try and put my sketch in a jpeg file on here before I have to go to the airport here in a minute... guess not;well if you play around with an 8" speaker and some cardboard,you should be able to make a decent pattern to make a box from. 
Z||000015||Racer 1||06-02-99||02:35 PM||||In my fiero I took out every crappy stock speaker and replaced the front 4-10" with kenwoods and installed one kenwood 6 1/2 in each of the doors and put polk audio 4-6" two way plates in back!for kenwood excelon 655 head unit with 10 disc changer goes to a xm-5 crossover to one rockford fosgate dsm 40 for the highs and a rockford fosgate punch 200 for the lows which consist of two 8"Bazooka base tubes positioned in front of each seat ... My system is the bomb!!ive gotten pulled over twice for nise voilation!!hehe 
Z||000016||zeusrekning||06-07-99||04:34 PM||||I was thinking about cutting my fire wall behind the seats and making a fiber glass enclouser for a 10" or a 12" sub behing each seat. I would rebuild the fire wall when the enclousers were in place. It would be like the back of the enclosure and the fire wall would be sealed into one. It's hard to explain but I have it fairly planned out. I would have to move some hoses and the battery.
Z||000017||TooLowFiero||06-08-99||11:35 PM||||ok  i am new but i thought ide tell ya what i did in my fiero  heres my system setup  pioneer cd player with ECQ pioneer indash 9 band parametric eq running to two amps and Alpine v-12 200 watt by two rms and an MTX thunder 2150 amp the alpine is pushing 2 MTX thunder 7000 10" subs in sealed boxes the mtx Amp is pushing 2 Blaupunkt threeway 6x9's in the dash 2 Kenwood tweeters 2 Polk Audio DX series 2 4x6's and get this ITS ALL IN THE CAB  now i dont know about you but 148db in the cab of a fiero is head turner only mods i made was the holes in the dash for the 6x9's  just thought i would share  TooLowFiero
